From 0357c9a20137726c094c2e9438cceac5a09195a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <ivanverbovoy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:55:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] view: a closed window fades and shrinks away rather than
 vanishing in a frame

At the unmap the view's last buffer - the client's, already a texture in
the renderer - is kept and drawn where the window was for 200 ms, alpha
1 -> 0 and scale 1 -> 0.92 about its centre, easing out, then let go.
Opening already fades a view in; closing did nothing. Whatever closed the
window goes the same way.
---
 src/meson.build  |   1 +
 src/render.c     |   3 +
 src/view-ghost.c | 309 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/view-ghost.h |  23 ++++
 src/view.c       |   5 +
 5 files changed, 341 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/view-ghost.c
 create mode 100644 src/view-ghost.h

